---
id: boiled-basmati-rice
title: Boiled Basmati Rice
category: modular_carb

yield:
  servings: 1
  cooked_g: 185

storage:
  fridge_days: 4
  freezer_friendly: true

---

Place @basmati-rice{0.33%cup} in a fine-mesh sieve and rinse under cold running water until the runoff is clear, removing excess surface starch so grains remain distinct and fluffy. Drain well.

In a #saucepan, combine the rinsed rice, 120 ml (1/2 cup) cold water, and @kosher-salt{0.25%tsp}. Bring to a rolling boil over medium-high heat.

Once boiling, immediately reduce heat to the lowest setting, cover tightly with a lid, and simmer undisturbed for ~simmer-time{11%min} until all water has been absorbed. Do not lift the lid or stir while cooking.

Remove the pot from the heat. Keep covered and let steam undisturbed for ~steam-time{5%min} to finish cooking and stabilize the grain structure.

Uncover and fluff gently with a fork. Transfer the cooked portion (185 g cooked yield) to a meal prep container and let cool before sealing.
